course: dictionary
lesson: 10670
title: Unmarried
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unmarried is an adjective. It means not married: an unmarried person does not have a husband or wife. The prefix un- means not, so unmarried is married with not in front of it, just like unhappy and untidy.
explain: «My aunt is unmarried, and she lives by the sea.» The word tells you about her marriage status, that she has no husband or wife. It does not tell you whether she is happy or sad.
explain: Forms often ask about your status, and the choices may be single, married, divorced or widowed. Single is the plain, everyday word for unmarried, so in a form or a story the two can mean the same thing.
fact: Unmarried means not married.
fact: The prefix un- means not, as in unhappy, untidy and unkind.
fact: «An unmarried aunt» means an aunt who does not have a husband or wife.
fact: «Natural child» means a child born to unmarried parents; this is an old-fashioned phrase used in the UK.
fact: Single is the plain word for unmarried, and forms may use either one.
exercise: «My aunt is unmarried.» What does unmarried mean here? | Lost and far from home | *Not married, with no husband or wife | Married twice | Very happy and calm
exercise: The prefix un- means what? | Very big | Again | Before | *Not
exercise: Which word means the same as unmarried on a form? | Widowed twice | *Single | Golden | Married and happy
test: «The unmarried couple bought a house together.» What does unmarried mean in this sentence? | *Not married, so they have no marriage | Tired from the walk | Very rich | Full of joy
test: Which word is the opposite of unmarried? | Single | Happy | *Married | Tidy
exam: In the phrase «natural child», what does unmarried mean? | Living in the country | Married and very proud | *Not married | Born in the winter
